    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-06T21:21:13+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-06T21:21:13+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-06T10:51:13Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-06T10:51:13Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">As a cold front clips the southeast Friday, while a high pressure system moves centred well south of Perth extends a ridge over northern and western SA. The high drifts over waters well to the south of SA over the weekend, while a developing low pressure system and trough in WA move close to the SA border. The high drifts southeast of Tasmania by Monday as the low moves across western SA on Monday and northern SA on Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW008" description="Mid North" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-06T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-06T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-06T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-07T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-06T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloud clearing. Winds southerly 15 to 25 km/h turning southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 10 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 23.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 10 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southeasterly 20 to 25 km/h turning easterly 25 to 35 km/h early in the morning then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 26.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. The chance of a thunderstorm in the north in the morning and afternoon. Winds northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h shifting west to southwesterly during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to around 14 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
